    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Digital Nomads Pickup Planning</h1>
    <p>Pickup day for a digital nomad is a logistics problem with a work calendar attached: the counter visit has to fit between calls, the first ride has to end at a known parking spot, and the machine that leaves the shop at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien has to be working infrastructure by Monday morning. Planned properly, pickup takes an afternoon and produces a month of commuting; improvised, it eats a working day and leaves questions unanswered in a saved-message thread. This page plans it properly, without inventing delivery arrangements, remote handovers or any service the shop has not verified itself.</p>
    <p>The page belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster, written for digital nomads. The verified fleet prices are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the long-stay terms the pickup conversation settles are covered in the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly rental hub</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Pickup as calendar engineering</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">Getting to Long Bien on a working day</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Choosing the hour inside 09:00 to 21:00</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">The counter conversation, nomad edition</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">The handover: photos, controls, fuel</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-6">The first commute and the first week</a></li>
